284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 160 0 R
/T (ABSTRACT)
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (Classroom mobile-phone use during teaching sessions can distract students and make it difficult for teachers to maintain continuous awareness of classroom activity. Conventional CCTV systems generally record video but do not automatically identify mobile phones or highlight possible usage events. This project proposes an AI-based smart classroom surveillance system that applies computer vision and deep learning to classroom video for mobile-phone detection.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The proposed workflow consists of five main modules: video acquisition and frame extraction, image preprocessing, mobile-phone detection using a YOLO object-detection model, mobile-phone usage assessment, and result visualization with alert generation. A camera or recorded classroom video supplies the input. The video is divided into frames at suitable intervals, and the frames are resized and prepared for model inference. The detection model identifies visible mobile phones and returns bounding boxes and confidence scores. Results across successive frames can then be examined to distinguish repeated appearances from brief or unclear detections. The system can display annotated frames and maintain event details such as timestamps and confidence values. Teacher notifications are an optional output where implemented.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The intended contribution is a structured, computer-vision-based support tool that reduces the effort required to review classroom footage and helps teachers locate possible phone-use events. The system is designed as an aid to human supervision rather than an automatic disciplinary decision-maker. Its practical performance will depend on camera position, lighting, occlusion, phone size, model training data, and processing hardware. Since the supplied project presentation describes the proposed architecture and modules but does not provide measured experimental results, numerical accuracy, latency, or deployment claims are not asserted here. These must be established through the test plan and recorded implementation evidence.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
