/T (Precision indicates the proportion of reported detections that are correct, while recall indicates the proportion of actual phone instances that are detected. Both are important: low precision can create unnecessary alerts, while low recall can cause relevant events to be missed. Processing speed should also be considered because a model that detects well but processes too slowly may not be suitable for live classroom use.)
/E (Precision indicates the proportion of reported detections that are correct, while recall indicates the proportion of actual phone instances that are detected. Both are important: low precision can create unnecessary alerts, while low recall can cause relevant events to be missed. Processing speed should also be considered because a model that detects well but processes too slowly may not be suitable for live classroom use.)
