933 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (This capstone project proposes an AI-based smart classroom surveillance workflow for detecting visible mobile phones in classroom video using computer vision and deep learning. The design combines video acquisition and frame extraction, image preprocessing, YOLO-based object detection, repeated-detection assessment, and result visualization with optional alert generation. The modular architecture provides a clear path for implementation and testing.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
934 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The proposed system can help teachers locate candidate phone-related events more efficiently than reviewing all recorded footage manually. However, a detection is only an indication that a phone may be visible; it is not proof of student behaviour or intent. Human review, privacy safeguards, and responsible use are essential. The supplied project materials do not contain measured implementation results, so the system's accuracy and real-time )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
